From: Ganesh Vernekar <ganesh.vernekar@reddit.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Feb 2026 12:35:26 -0800
Subject: Kubernetes SD: Disable WatchListClient in tests

client-go v0.35.0+ enables the WatchListClient feature gate by default.
The fake clientset used in the discovery/kubernetes tests does not send
the initial-events-end bookmark, so informers never sync and the tests
time out with "discoverer failed to sync". Debian's golang-k8s-client-go
0.36.4 triggers this.

Backported by Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me> without
the unrelated NewSimpleClientset -> NewClientset change.

Origin: backport, https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/commit/847e474bf4ffe637f1e6c9317f81d78015e40b7a
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1147746
Applied-Upstream: 3.10.0
Reviewed-by: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Last-Update: 2026-09-14
---
Index: prometheus/discovery/kubernetes/kubernetes_test.go
===================================================================
--- prometheus.orig/discovery/kubernetes/kubernetes_test.go
+++ prometheus/discovery/kubernetes/kubernetes_test.go
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ import (
 	"context"
 	"encoding/json"
 	"errors"
+	"os"
 	"testing"
 	"time"
 
@@ -42,6 +43,14 @@ import (
 )
 
 func TestMain(m *testing.M) {
+	// Disable the WatchListClient feature gate that is enabled by default in
+	// client-go v0.35.0+. The WatchList flow requires the server to support
+	// SendInitialEvents and to send a bookmark event with the
+	// "k8s.io/initial-events-end" annotation. The fake clientset used in tests
+	// does not support this protocol, causing informers to hang indefinitely
+	// waiting for the bookmark. Disabling this feature restores the traditional
+	// List+Watch flow which is compatible with the fake clientset.
+	os.Setenv("KUBE_FEATURE_WatchListClient", "false")
 	testutil.TolerantVerifyLeak(m)
 }
 
